# PDF Builder — ready-to-run requests.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above any block.
# Rider and Visual Studio open .http files natively.
#
# Set @host to 8080 when running under Docker, and @apiKey to a key issued with admin.http.

@host = http://localhost:5052

# A key with pdf:generate, issued with admin.http. Under Docker the published local-only admin key
# from compose.yaml works too. Health checks need no key, and a file link is its own credential.
@apiKey = pdf_paste-your-key-here

# The admin key, only for the last request in this file: the operator acting as a client. Under Docker it is the
# published local-only one from compose.yaml.
@adminKey = adm_lPQ25ykvuTW7HdOJLaJzfqnJsT4cKQfwwR5pgq4o


### Liveness — the process is up. Works with no broker.
GET {{host}}/health/live


### Readiness — the broker is connected and the template directory exists.
# 503 here with everything else working almost always means RabbitMQ is unreachable.
GET {{host}}/health/ready


### Happy path — the full sample invoice.
# @name enqueue
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateKey": "invoice",
  "data": {
    "seller":   { "name": "Circle360", "address": "12 Nile Street, Cairo, Egypt", "tax_id": "100-200-300" },
    "customer": { "name": "Acme Trading LLC", "address": "44 Market Road, Dubai, UAE" },
    "invoice": {
      "number": "INV-2026-0041",
      "issued_on": "2026-10-01",
      "due_on": "2026-10-31",
      "currency": "USD",
      "notes": "Payment due within 30 days. Late payments accrue 1.5% monthly interest."
    },
    "items": [
      { "description": "Platform subscription - October", "quantity": 1,  "unit_price": 1200.00 },
      { "description": "Additional seats",                "quantity": 12, "unit_price": 25.00 },
      { "description": "Onboarding workshop",             "quantity": 2,  "unit_price": 450.00 }
    ],
    "totals": { "subtotal": 2400.00, "tax": 336.00, "total": 2736.00 }
  }
}


### Poll the job from the request above. `fileUrl` is the link to the PDF.
# With Blocks:Files:RequireSignature on it is signed and `fileUrlExpiresAt` says when it stops working;
# with it off it is the plain /files/{fileId} and the expiry is null. Use it as-is.
# @name status
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{enqueue.response.body.jobId}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Download the PDF with the link from the status. No key: the link is the credential.
# After its expiry (signing on), or once the file is deleted, this is a bare 404: ask for a fresh link below.
GET {{status.response.body.fileUrl}}


### Files — a fresh link for a job you own. Earlier links keep working until their own expiry.
# @name freshLink
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{enqueue.response.body.jobId}}/file-url
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Files — download straight from the API with your key, no link involved.
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{enqueue.response.body.jobId}}/file
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Files — 409 JOB_HAS_NO_FILE: the job failed (see the missing-template request below), so there is no file.
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{missingTemplate.response.body.jobId}}/file-url
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Files — 410 FILE_EXPIRED: the file was deleted after Blocks:Files:RetentionDays.
# Answered for an old job whose file is gone; the job's own status then says "fileExpired": true.
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{enqueue.response.body.jobId}}/file-url
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Minimal payload — every optional field omitted.
# No tax_id, no notes, no tax line. Those sections should simply not appear.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateKey": "invoice",
  "data": {
    "seller":   { "name": "Circle360", "address": "12 Nile Street, Cairo" },
    "customer": { "name": "Walk-in Customer", "address": "-" },
    "invoice":  { "number": "INV-0001", "issued_on": "2026-10-07", "due_on": "2026-10-07", "currency": "EGP" },
    "items":    [ { "description": "One-off service", "quantity": 1, "unit_price": 500 } ],
    "totals":   { "subtotal": 500, "total": 500 }
  }
}


### Same invoice on Letter paper, landscape — page setup for this request only.
# The template's margins are kept; only what is named here changes.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateKey": "invoice",
  "pageSetup": { "format": "Letter", "landscape": true },
  "data": {
    "seller":   { "name": "Circle360", "address": "12 Nile Street, Cairo" },
    "customer": { "name": "Walk-in Customer", "address": "-" },
    "invoice":  { "number": "INV-0001", "issued_on": "2026-10-07", "due_on": "2026-10-07", "currency": "EGP" },
    "items":    [ { "description": "One-off service", "quantity": 1, "unit_price": 500 } ],
    "totals":   { "subtotal": 500, "total": 500 }
  }
}


### A malformed page setup — expect 400 naming pageSetup.Width and pageSetup.Height.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateKey": "invoice",
  "pageSetup": { "width": "80" },
  "data": { "a": 1 }
}


### Empty item list — exercises the template's `else` branch.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateKey": "invoice",
  "data": {
    "seller":   { "name": "Circle360", "address": "12 Nile Street, Cairo" },
    "customer": { "name": "Acme Trading LLC", "address": "44 Market Road, Dubai" },
    "invoice":  { "number": "INV-EMPTY", "issued_on": "2026-10-07", "due_on": "2026-11-07", "currency": "USD" },
    "items":    [],
    "totals":   { "subtotal": 0, "total": 0 }
  }
}


### Number handling — money keeps its decimals, big integers stay readable.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateKey": "invoice",
  "data": {
    "seller":   { "name": "Circle360", "address": "12 Nile Street, Cairo" },
    "customer": { "name": "Precision Test Co", "address": "Nowhere" },
    "invoice":  { "number": "INV-PRECISION", "issued_on": "2026-10-07", "due_on": "2026-11-07", "currency": "USD" },
    "items": [
      { "description": "Exact decimal", "quantity": 3,   "unit_price": 0.1 },
      { "description": "Large value",   "quantity": 1,   "unit_price": 1234567890.12 },
      { "description": "Fractional qty","quantity": 2.5, "unit_price": 40 }
    ],
    "totals": { "subtotal": 1234567990.42, "total": 1234567990.42 }
  }
}


# ───────────────────────── failure cases ─────────────────────────
# The first three are refused at the edge and need no broker at all.

### 400 — template key could escape the template directory.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "../../etc/passwd", "data": {} }


### 400 — data is an array, not an object.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "invoice", "data": [1, 2, 3] }


### 400 — template key is missing.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "anything": true } }


### 202, then the job fails with TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND.
# Well-formed, so it is queued; the worker is what discovers there is no such template.
# @name missingTemplate
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "does-not-exist", "data": { "anything": true } }


### Poll it — expect "Failed" with errorCode TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND.
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{missingTemplate.response.body.jobId}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### 404 — a job id nobody issued.
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### 404 — a file id that is not one we hand out. Also what every altered, expired or unsigned link gets.
GET {{host}}/files/not-a-real-file-id


### 401 AUTH_REQUIRED — no key. Every /api call needs one.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "invoice", "data": {} }


### 401 AUTH_INVALID_KEY — a key that was never issued. Revoked and expired keys answer exactly the same.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: pdf_zzzzzzzz_notarealsecret0000000000000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "invoice", "data": {} }


### ===== Two clients: templates and jobs belong to the client whose key made them ==================
# Register two clients, `ecommerce` and `erp`, and issue each a key with all three pdf:* permissions
# (admin.http), then paste the keys here. Another client's template or job answers 404, exactly as one
# that does not exist. The built-in templates (`invoice`) are everybody's.

@ecommerceKey = pdf_paste-the-ecommerce-key-here
@erpKey = pdf_paste-the-erp-key-here


### 1. ecommerce creates a template called `statement`...
POST {{host}}/api/templates
X-Api-Key: {{ecommerceKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "statement", "content": { "html": "<p>The ecommerce statement</p>", "css": "", "sampleJson": "{}" } }


### ...and publishes it, so jobs can render it.
POST {{host}}/api/templates/statement/publish
X-Api-Key: {{ecommerceKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "revision": 1 }


### 2. erp lists templates: no `statement`, but the built-in `invoice` is there.
GET {{host}}/api/templates
X-Api-Key: {{erpKey}}


### 3. erp reads it: 404 TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND, the same answer as for a key nobody has.
GET {{host}}/api/templates/statement
X-Api-Key: {{erpKey}}


### 4. erp creates its own `statement`: 201. The same key, a different template, changed independently.
POST {{host}}/api/templates
X-Api-Key: {{erpKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "statement", "content": { "html": "<p>The erp statement</p>", "css": "", "sampleJson": "{}" } }


### ...and publishes it.
POST {{host}}/api/templates/statement/publish
X-Api-Key: {{erpKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "revision": 1 }


### 5. Each submits a job for `statement`. Each renders its own client's template.
# @name ecommerceJob
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{ecommerceKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "statement", "data": {} }


###
# @name erpJob
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{erpKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "statement", "data": {} }


### 6. erp reads ecommerce's job: 404, as for an id nobody issued. ecommerce reads its own as usual.
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{ecommerceJob.response.body.jobId}}
X-Api-Key: {{erpKey}}


###
GET {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs/{{ecommerceJob.response.body.jobId}}
X-Api-Key: {{ecommerceKey}}


### The operator works inside one client at a time. With the admin key, say which: no X-Client-Id is a 400
# asking for one, an unregistered one is 404 CLIENT_NOT_FOUND, and a disabled one still works.
GET {{host}}/api/templates
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
X-Client-Id: ecommerce
